From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ys@ys.contact>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:18:23 -0400
Subject: fix: the owner's Mac pass on beta 10

The owner used beta 10 on their own Arc-imported profile and found
these, fixed here:

- Restored tabs came back as crashed pages. A tab created unloaded,
  as the Arc import creates them, never commits, so its frame entry
  has sequence numbers of -1. The session saved them in the page
  state, Blink keeps any non-zero number, and after a restart the
  document committed with -1, which the browser kills as a bad
  message (RFH_INVALID_DOCUMENT_SEQUENCE_NUMBER). NavigationEntryImpl
  now writes a missing number as 0, Blink's "none", and reads a saved
  negative one as 0 (import I26).
- The address row hid with the sidebar, which read as the address bar
  disappearing. The setting is now off by default (toolbar T8, T12).
- The row's colour was often not the page's: pages paint their top
  with layers their declared colour knows nothing of. The row now
  takes the colour the page draws along its top edge when that edge
  is one colour, then the theme colour, then the background (T31).
  In macOS full screen the overlay paints the row in the page's
  colour too; it was the bare ground there (T32).
- The Space swipe switched at a fixed distance with nothing moving.
  The title and the list now follow the fingers, the lift switches or
  springs back, and the next Space slides in from the side the
  fingers left (spaces B35).
- The switcher turned to dots with room left for every chip. The gaps
  close up to 4 DIP first (spaces B24).

The Mac then used the build on a copy of that profile and on a fresh
one, with the real pointer and keyboard, and found these, fixed here
too:

- On saturated pages the row was a step off the page's colour. The
  page's top is read back in the display's colour space, Display P3
  on a Mac's own screen, and was painted as if it were sRGB, so the
  colour went to P3 twice. The strip is read as sRGB now (T31).
- In full screen a second, darker line sat under the row's hairline:
  Chromium's separator for its slide-in toolbar. It is not drawn for
  Stedding's window (T32).
- A Space switch on the owner's profile, hundreds of tabs, showed
  nothing for half a second. The Space's tint re-themes every row of
  every Space; each row set its title's font again, and a label asks
  for a layout whenever its font is set, so the whole list was laid
  out once per row, and each row in a folder drew the folder's glyph
  from macOS's symbol again. A row sets its font only when it changed
  and the glyph is drawn once per colour and size (spaces B36).
- In the rail the Clear line's label was drawn clipped to "lear". The
  line is drawn alone there, with no press (spaces B17).
- In light mode a folder's name and glyph, white for the dark ground,
  were nearly invisible. They take the rows' own text colour
  (folders F12).

What that pass logged rather than fixed before beta 11, fixed here:

- A Space switch opened each incoming row from collapsed under the
  slide, the rows squeezed together for its first 50 ms. The rows take
  their places at once and only the list moves (spaces B37).
- Cmd-T from an empty New Tab page opened a second tab and left the
  empty one in the list. An untouched New Tab page takes what the bar
  opens, as Arc's does (commandbar K21).
- The Clear line all but vanished on a tinted Space. It is the rows'
  text colour at a quarter strength (spaces B17).
- The welcome flow's import step ran under its footer with nothing to
  say it scrolled, and its keys step ran 16 DIP under it. A step that
  runs on fades out at the bottom (welcome W11), and the keys step no
  longer teaches Peek's Cmd-O, which is withdrawn (W6).
- Arc, while it runs, takes Opt-Cmd-N from every app; the shortcut
  reference in Settings says so (shortcuts Z3).

Why: the owner's own use of beta 10 on 2026-10-01 and the Mac's pass
on a copy of their profile on 2026-10-02 (docs/ARC-ROUND2.md, round
11); each finding is a behaviour in its feature's spec.
Removable when: the Phase 4 re-cut (PLAN.md SER-4) folds these fixes
into the feature patches they belong to.
